						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Okay, Arme, you want an answer? Read this closely.  <br />
<br />
You were deliberately and childishly interfering with someone else's quest last night.  This is not only conduct unbecoming one of my officers, but it is a bannable offense.  I watched you attack the named mob, which you were repeatedly asked you not to, simply because you believed you were wronged by someone's not answering your question.  No, you didn't kill the mob, but I asked you to leave the mob alone and let them complete their quest and then resume your quest. You chose to do otherwise.<br />
<br />
I won't deny you've done a lot for the guild.  Hell, I fought for keeping you in the guild when some of your personal problems leaked into game play when Ciervox was still running The Ancients.  I have overlooked reports of bad manners, vulgarity and other disruptive behaviors.  But your actions were particularly vexxing and you could not see that you had handled the entire situation badly.<br />
<br />
The actions of each guildmember often reflect on the guild itself.  The actions of officers represent the guild; as such, I hold my officers to a higher standard of conduct.<br />
<br />
You may not agree that what you did was wrong, but I suggest you read the Play Nice rules which are part of what you agree to each time you sign onto the game.<br />
If you dispute this, ask a GM. <br />
<br />
While the guild rules have been removed from the guildnews page on this site, you did certify that you read and understood them.  I expected you to follow both sets of rules, but last night this proved too much for you.<br />
<br />
You may think you're deserving of a hearing and you may think you have some kind of appeal process.  If you can gather 10% support from the guild (that's 20 members), I'll reinstate you as a regular member.  I think I'm being more than generous for making this offer.  <br />
<br />
If this happens, I will expect you to behave in a far more mature manner than I have seen.<br />
<br />
Ollie						</td>
